434
00:16:23,173 --> 00:16:25,193
Here is the first common mistake.

435
00:16:25,373 --> 00:16:27,664
Buyers pick the truck from a list,

436
00:16:27,664 --> 00:16:30,427
and then walk into the dealership without

437
00:16:30,427 --> 00:16:30,899
a plan.

438
00:16:31,079 --> 00:16:34,016
The salesperson talks about the monthly payment.

439
00:16:34,196 --> 00:16:37,370
The better question is the out-the-door price,

440
00:16:37,370 --> 00:16:40,405
which includes the destination fee and every

441
00:16:40,405 --> 00:16:41,302
other charge.

442
00:16:41,482 --> 00:16:43,555
Ask for it in writing for two

443
00:16:43,555 --> 00:16:45,272
trucks of the same trim,

444
00:16:45,272 --> 00:16:46,416
on the same day.

445
00:16:46,596 --> 00:16:48,662
Then compare those two numbers.

446
00:16:48,842 --> 00:16:51,291
That is the only comparison that is

447
00:16:51,291 --> 00:16:51,640
fair.

448
00:16:51,991 --> 00:16:55,195
The second mistake is trusting one source.

449
00:16:55,375 --> 00:16:57,515
We showed that the Ram is first

450
00:16:57,515 --> 00:16:59,724
in one study and near the bottom

451
00:16:59,724 --> 00:17:00,483
in another.

452
00:17:00,663 --> 00:17:02,964
A buyer who reads only the first

453
00:17:02,964 --> 00:17:05,911
source will buy with too much confidence.

454
00:17:06,091 --> 00:17:08,682
A buyer who reads only the second

455
00:17:08,682 --> 00:17:11,352
will miss a truck that owners rate

456
00:17:11,352 --> 00:17:11,745
well.

457
00:17:11,925 --> 00:17:14,733
Read both, write down what each one

458
00:17:14,733 --> 00:17:18,023
measures, and then decide how much weight

459
00:17:18,023 --> 00:17:19,146
each deserves.

460
00:17:19,326 --> 00:17:21,717
Doing that takes ten minutes and can

461
00:17:21,717 --> 00:17:23,111
save a lot of regret.

462
00:17:23,462 --> 00:17:24,994
So who should wait?

463
00:17:25,174 --> 00:17:27,517
If you are thinking about the Santa

464
00:17:27,517 --> 00:17:28,923
Cruz style of buying,

465
00:17:28,923 --> 00:17:31,601
where the model has an uncertain future,

466
00:17:31,601 --> 00:17:34,011
wait until you know what the company

467
00:17:34,011 --> 00:17:34,346
says.

468
00:17:34,526 --> 00:17:35,944
If you want a Ram,

469
00:17:35,944 --> 00:17:39,017
wait until you have checked the recalls

470
00:17:39,017 --> 00:17:41,696
and the ABS software issue for the

471
00:17:41,696 --> 00:17:43,036
exact model year.

472
00:17:43,216 --> 00:17:44,921
And if you want the Tundra,

473
00:17:44,921 --> 00:17:47,005
wait until you have looked at the

474
00:17:47,005 --> 00:17:48,963
engine record and the warranty.

475
00:17:49,143 --> 00:17:51,430
Waiting a week to check is cheap.

476
00:17:51,610 --> 00:17:54,080
Owning the wrong truck for five years

477
00:17:54,080 --> 00:17:54,547
is not.

478
00:17:54,898 --> 00:17:56,465
And who should buy now?

479
00:17:56,645 --> 00:17:59,678
A first-time buyer who wants low running

480
00:17:59,678 --> 00:18:01,801
costs and a low price can go

481
00:18:01,801 --> 00:18:04,227
straight to the Maverick Hybrid,

482
00:18:04,227 --> 00:18:06,502
because the numbers are clear.

483
00:18:06,682 --> 00:18:08,860
A buyer who wants a truck that

484
00:18:08,860 --> 00:18:10,022
holds its value,

485
00:18:10,022 --> 00:18:12,274
and does not need heavy towing,

486
00:18:12,274 --> 00:18:13,799
can go to the Tacoma.

487
00:18:13,979 --> 00:18:16,306
A buyer who tows or hauls for

488
00:18:16,306 --> 00:18:19,115
a living can look at the heavy-duty

489
00:18:19,115 --> 00:18:21,923
group, and think about the truck as

490
00:18:21,923 --> 00:18:24,010
a tool, not an investment.

491
00:18:24,190 --> 00:18:26,645
Each of these buyers can decide with

492
00:18:26,645 --> 00:18:29,577
confidence, because the data fits the need.

493
00:18:29,927 --> 00:18:32,035
How do you check a recall in

494
00:18:32,035 --> 00:18:32,713
practice?

495
00:18:32,893 --> 00:18:35,622
Take the vehicle identification number,

496
00:18:35,622 --> 00:18:38,071
the VIN, from the windshield or the

497
00:18:38,071 --> 00:18:40,380
door sticker, and enter it in the

498
00:18:40,380 --> 00:18:43,388
official recall lookup from the government.

499
00:18:43,568 --> 00:18:45,830
It tells you whether a repair is

500
00:18:45,830 --> 00:18:47,597
open on that exact truck.

501
00:18:47,777 --> 00:18:49,621
Do this for a new truck on

502
00:18:49,621 --> 00:18:51,464
the lot, as well as a used

503
00:18:51,464 --> 00:18:51,748
one.

504
00:18:51,928 --> 00:18:53,187
For a used truck,

505
00:18:53,187 --> 00:18:55,781
also ask the seller for the service

506
00:18:55,781 --> 00:18:58,671
records, and ask for the warranty terms

507
00:18:58,671 --> 00:18:59,486
in writing.

508
00:18:59,666 --> 00:19:00,900
It costs nothing,

509
00:19:00,900 --> 00:19:03,296
and it is the best protection you

510
00:19:03,296 --> 00:19:03,660
have.

511
00:19:04,010 --> 00:19:06,826
One more honest point about the heavy-duty

512
00:19:06,826 --> 00:19:07,295
trucks.

513
00:19:07,475 --> 00:19:09,266
They hold their value,

514
00:19:09,266 --> 00:19:10,080
